Ticket **#4471** was marked known as a single parser bug. The export disagrees: the same
412 reports split into two causes once you look up each tenant's locale and booking form
(`#lib/kb/causes`).

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Two causes share this ticket; only the majority cause belongs here.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets filed

| cause | reports | GitHub issue | fix |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | shared parser reads month first; day-first tenants flip | keep #4471 for this cause |
| `hint` | 33 | booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while the tenant is day-first | needs its own ticket |

The five reports the desk read as a one-day move stay under `parser` by tenant; they are
footnoted in the table above, not a third cause.

## Why the merge failed

Intake tags and subject-line dedupe ([0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) do not see
the tenant form. Form traffic on booking-v3 looks like the parser bug and lands in the same
subject bucket, so it was merged into #4471 with no ticket of its own.

